<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siad Barre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1995">1995</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mohamed Siad Barre</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siad Barre was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> army general who seized power in a coup on 21 October 1969, days after the assassination of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdirashid-ali-shermarke">Abdirashid Ali Shermarke</a>, and ruled the Somali Democratic Republic until 1991. He proclaimed scientific socialism and introduced a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> script for Somali, but defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ogaden-war">Ogaden War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> in 1977–1978 and clan-based repression led to civil war and his overthrow.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siad-barre.jpg" alt="Siad Barre" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of Somalia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Official_portrait_of_Major_General_Siad_Barre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under the military regime of <b>Siad Barre</b>, which seized power in 1969, opposition grew among the Isaaq, the largest clan family in the north, and in 1981 exiles in London founded the Somali National Movement (SNM).</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-somaliland">Republic of Somaliland · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>On 21 October 1969, days after the assassination of President Abdirashid Ali Shermarke, the army led by <b>Mohamed Siad Barre</b> seized power in the Somali Republic.</blockquote><a href="/state/somali-democratic-republic">Somali Democratic Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>On 15 October 1969 Shermarke was assassinated, and six days later the army under <b>Mohamed Siad Barre</b> seized power, dissolving parliament and creating the Somali Democratic Republic.</blockquote><a href="/state/somali-republic">Somali Republic</a></li><li><blockquote>When <b>Siad Barre</b> fled in January 1991, the Somali Democratic Republic collapsed.</blockquote><a href="/state/somalia">Somalia</a></li></ul></section>
